From k384 (2026-10-31). k384 covered ocp status, node ls, health and provider ls (OCP::Role::Cmd::reach_cluster_api / cluster_api_unreachable). The same client build and the same 599 death, with LWP source locations and OCP.pm's internal-error label, remain in: Node::TrustHost, Node::Add, OCP::Role::Cmd::Machines, Destroy (k353's file), Apply's _k8s_api, and SSH.pm. Done = each says the k384 line (one helper call, or a catch with cluster_api_unreachable where the command has its own fallback, e.g. destroy's and ssh's API cascades must keep going), and a test per command against a closed local port. Several lanes: split per owning worker when dispatched, after k375, k353 and k306 2b (same files).

After k387: the helpers are OCP::Role::Cmd cluster_api_error (any APIError -> one line) and cluster_api_call (runs one call, dies with that line); cluster_api_unreachable is gone. reach_cluster_api now treats any error status at /version as fatal. Use these for TrustHost.pm:49, Node/Add.pm:132, Role/Cmd/Machines.pm:217.

Stopped right after dispatch (2026-10-31): the maintainer wants to look at abstracting the cluster API client build across commands first; per-site fixes would be superseded.

Destroy's part (from k382, destroy worker): the _cluster_api eval only builds the client; the API calls are at Destroy.pm:343 (_ocpnode_entries' own eval, prints the raw error), :357 (provider_crs, outside any eval) and :767 (_stop_robocop, raw error). Destroy does not die on a closed port.

